From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 06:30:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 10/10] container_manager: leave the host's nfcd alone

Starting the container runs "systemctl stop nfcd", and only stopping it
again starts nfcd back up. That is upstream handing the host's NFC
controller to Android. On LuneOS the controller stays with the host -
webos-nfc-adapter drives it through nfcd, and 0008 already stops the
container from claiming NFC - so this only takes NFC away from the host.

It is worse when the container fails to start: nothing ever runs the
matching start, and NFC stays dead until the next boot. Seen on a Minimal
Phone MP01: nfcd registered its adapter at boot and was stopped three
minutes later, the moment a Waydroid session was started.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [LuneOS keeps NFC on the host]

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
---
--- a/tools/actions/container_manager.py
+++ b/tools/actions/container_manager.py
@@ -190,14 +190,6 @@
             if os.path.exists("/sys/fs/cgroup/schedtune/probe0"):
                 os.rmdir("/sys/fs/cgroup/schedtune/probe0")
 
-    #TODO: remove NFC hacks
-    if which("stop"):
-        command = ["stop", "nfcd"]
-        tools.helpers.run.user(args, command, check=False)
-    elif which("systemctl") and (tools.helpers.run.user(args, ["systemctl", "is-active", "-q", "nfcd"], check=False) == 0):
-        command = ["systemctl", "stop", "nfcd"]
-        tools.helpers.run.user(args, command, check=False)
-
     # Set permissions
     set_permissions(args)
 
@@ -239,14 +231,6 @@
                    "/data/scripts/waydroid-net.sh", "stop"]
         tools.helpers.run.user(args, command, check=False)
 
-        #TODO: remove NFC hacks
-        if which("start"):
-            command = ["start", "nfcd"]
-            tools.helpers.run.user(args, command, check=False)
-        elif which("systemctl") and (tools.helpers.run.user(args, ["systemctl", "is-enabled", "-q", "nfcd"], check=False) == 0):
-            command = ["systemctl", "start", "nfcd"]
-            tools.helpers.run.user(args, command, check=False)
-
         # Sensors
         if which("waydroid-sensord"):
             command = ["pidof", "waydroid-sensord"]
